{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The deviation is established on the platform's recorded distances, not on the trace: actual 16.80 km less optimal 15.30 km is 1.50 km, which is above POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance. POL-RD-22 uses the trip record's distances precisely because a sparse trace understates a route's length, and this 59-fix trace measures only 14.177 km — below the recommended route length — so it cannot be used to re-measure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-06003", "EV-GPS-06003"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.deviation_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver gave notice before the point of deviation. His in-app message MSG-06003-003 was sent at 17:55:39 and read at 17:55:48: 'Hi, accident on ECP after Marine Parade, I exit Fort Road and go Marine Parade Road instead ok?' The route_deviation_detected event is timestamped 17:58:49, over three minutes later, so the POL-RD-21 obligation to inform the rider 'before or at the point of deviation' is met, and no verbal notice or call recording is needed because the chat log carries the notice.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-06003", "EV-TRIP-06003"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.messages_during_trip",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider acknowledged the deviation before it happened: her reply MSG-06003-004, 'Sure no problem', was sent at 17:56:14, again before the 17:58:49 deviation point. Under POL-RD-21, where the chat log confirms the rider's acknowledgment the deviation is agreed, and this chat log is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 and reconciles to trip_record.chat_message_count of 4.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-06003", "EV-TRIP-06003"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The reroute was traffic-justified. LTA advisory LTA-TI-260923-1113 records an ACCIDENT on the East Coast Parkway (towards Changi) after the Marine Parade exit, issued 17:34:22 and valid to 18:49:22 — overlapping the trip window of 17:49:22 to 18:18:22. ACCIDENT is within POL-RD-23's admissible 'incident' vocabulary, and the artifact is a third-party traffic record, not the driver's assertion.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-06003-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The advisory sits on the recommended route. Its own fields give road 'East Coast Parkway (ECP)', direction 'towards Changi' and location 'after Marine Parade exit' — the same road and the same direction of travel that the recommended route lists ('North Bridge Road, Raffles Avenue, East Coast Parkway (ECP), Bedok South Road, Simei Street 3'). The driver's contemporaneous message independently names the same incident, 'accident on ECP after Marine Parade'. The artifact flags route intersection as 'undetermined' and leaves it to the Judge; nothing in the record places the advisory anywhere other than the ECP carriageway the recommended route uses towards this dropoff.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-06003-01", "EV-CHAT-06003", "EV-TRIP-06003"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On POL-RD-24's matrix this case falls in row (a): the reroute was traffic-justified, the rider was informed and agreed, and the deviation was over 1 km. Row (a) pays no refund, so the outcome is NO_ACTION. Rows (b) and (d) are the refund rows, and neither applies once justification and the rider's agreement are established.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-06003", "EV-CHAT-06003", "EV-ADVIS-06003-01", "EV-FARE-06003"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's figure of 5.00 SGD is unsupported on the policy's own arithmetic even on the reading most favourable to her. The only refund available on this matrix is the excess distance fare: 1.50 km x 0.72 SGD per km = 1.08 SGD, with no surge applied. Row (b) or (d) would therefore move 1.08 SGD, not 5.00 SGD, and the rider's claim for the balance fails in any event.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-06003", "EV-TRIP-06003"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "NO_ACTION is the driver's outcome here. The rider filed this dispute, the fare stands charged at 26.04 SGD and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00; POL-GEN-03 makes NO_ACTION party-relative and it preserves the present state, leaving the metered fare the driver earned intact rather than restoring anything.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-06003"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no open question requiring escalation under POL-GEN-26. Each fact POL-RD-24 needs — the deviation distance, the notice to the rider, the rider's agreement and the traffic justification — is carried by a COMPLETE artifact at weight_multiplier 1.0, so POL-GEN-02 caps nothing and the record is sufficient for a ruling.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-06003", "EV-CHAT-06003", "EV-GPS-06003", "EV-ADVIS-06003-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To both parties: this is decided on the platform's own records, and the rider's claim is not supported. The present state stands.\n\nThe deviation is real, and I accept it. POL-RD-22 measures it from the trip record's recorded distances, not from the trace: 16.80 km actual less 15.30 km recommended is 1.50 km, above the 1.0 km tolerance. Both sides agree on this, and the GPS trace (which measures only 14.177 km) is not used to re-measure, exactly as POL-RD-22 provides.\n\nThe reroute was traffic-justified under POL-RD-23. LTA advisory LTA-TI-260923-1113 records an ACCIDENT on the East Coast Parkway (towards Changi) after the Marine Parade exit, valid 17:34:22 to 18:49:22, and so overlapping the trip window (17:49:22 to 18:18:22). ACCIDENT is an admissible 'incident' type. The advisory's road (ECP), direction (towards Changi) and location (after Marine Parade exit) place it on the recommended route's ECP segment, which the recommended route uses from Raffles Avenue through to Bedok South Road; the recommended route does not leave the ECP until Bedok South Road, so an incident after the Marine Parade exit lies on it. The artifact leaves intersection 'undetermined' for the Judge, and on these fields I decide it intersects. The rider's point that the message says 'avoid lanes 2 and 3' does not change this: POL-RD-23 asks whether the advisory intersects the route and shows an incident, not whether the road was impassable.\n\nThe driver informed the rider before the deviation, and the rider agreed. MSG-06003-003 was sent at 17:55:39 and read at 17:55:48; MSG-06003-004, 'Sure no problem', was sent at 17:56:14; the route_deviation_detected event is at 17:58:49. POL-RD-21's notice was therefore given before the point of deviation, and the chat log confirms the rider's acknowledgment, so the deviation is agreed.\n\nOn POL-RD-24 exactly one row applies, and it is row (a): traffic-justified, rider informed and agreed, deviation over 1 km — no refund. Rows (b) and (d) are the refund rows and neither applies. The rider's stated figure of 5.00 SGD is unsupported in any event: the only refund the matrix ever yields is the excess distance fare, which on these figures would be 1.50 km x 0.72 SGD per km = 1.08 SGD, with no surge. The rider filed this dispute, so under POL-GEN-03 NO_ACTION is read against her claim and leaves the metered fare of 26.04 SGD charged and refund_issued_sgd of 0.00 undisturbed; it restores nothing to the driver.\n\nThe rider's alternative — that the traffic element is unestablished and the case must be escalated under POL-GEN-26 — fails. The fact POL-RD-23 needs is carried by a COMPLETE artifact at weight_multiplier 1.0 (EV-ADVIS-06003-01), and it is established from that artifact's own fields; there is no missing or impaired evidence and so no open question. POL-RD-25's 0.80 confidence requirement is met at 0.85, and POL-GEN-22 (5.00 SGD contested, below the 10.00 SGD band, no fraud flags) permits the AI ruling to stand.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim is that the driver left the East Coast Parkway and drove through Marine Parade, and that you were overcharged. The deviation itself is made out on the platform's own recorded distances: the trip record shows an actual route of 16.80 km against a recommended 15.30 km, a difference of 1.50 km, above POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance (the trace is deliberately not used to re-measure distance, because a 59-fix trace understates route length). So the first part of your account is accepted. To the driver: the reroute is nonetheless not refundable, and the fare of 26.04 SGD stands.\n\nWhy no refund, on POL-RD-24's matrix. Three elements are each carried by a complete artifact at weight 1.0. (1) Traffic justification under POL-RD-23: LTA advisory LTA-TI-260923-1113 records an ACCIDENT on the East Coast Parkway (towards Changi) after the Marine Parade exit, valid 17:34:22 to 18:49:22, overlapping the trip window of 17:49:22 to 18:18:22. ACCIDENT is within the clause's 'incident' vocabulary. The advisory's intersection with the recommended route was left 'undetermined' by the pre-pass and is mine to decide from its road, direction and location against the trip: its road is the ECP and its direction is towards Changi — the very carriageway and direction the recommended route uses ('North Bridge Road, Raffles Avenue, East Coast Parkway (ECP), Bedok South Road, Simei Street 3') — and its location, after the Marine Parade exit, falls on the ECP stretch between the Fort Road exit and the Bedok South Road rejoin that the driver bypassed. It therefore intersects the recommended route and the reroute is traffic-justified. Your point that the advisory only says 'Avoid lanes 2 and 3' and so left the ECP open does not assist: POL-RD-23 requires data showing congestion, an incident or a closure, not that the road be shut. (2) Notice under POL-RD-21: the driver's in-app message MSG-06003-003, sent 17:55:39 and read 17:55:48 — 'Hi, accident on ECP after Marine Parade, I exit Fort Road and go Marine Parade Road instead ok?' — precedes the route_deviation_detected event at 17:58:49, so notice was given before the point of deviation, and it gave a reason, which is enough. (3) Agreement: your reply MSG-06003-004, 'Sure no problem', sent 17:56:14, also before 17:58:49, is the acknowledgment POL-RD-21 looks for in the chat log.\n\nOn that combination the case is row (a) of POL-RD-24 — traffic-justified, rider informed and agreed, deviation over 1 km — which pays no refund. Rows (b) and (d), the refund rows, do not apply. For completeness, even on the reading most favourable to you the policy's measure would have been the excess distance fare only: 1.50 km x 0.72 SGD per km = 1.08 SGD, without surge, not the 5.00 SGD you asked for; but no such refund arises here.\n\nI have also considered the argument that the advisory's route intersection cannot be established and that POL-GEN-26 therefore requires escalation, with POL-RD-25's 0.80 confidence bar said to be unreachable on NO_ACTION. That argument fails at its first step: the intersection is establishable from the advisory's own road, direction and location against the recommended route, as set out above, so there is no fact the record leaves unestablished, no open question to state, and no escalation. The rider's own acknowledgment does not itself supply the justification — that is right — but the justification is supplied independently by the LTA advisory, so row (a) is reached on its own terms rather than through your agreement.\n\nOutcome: the rider's claim is not supported and the present state stands. Both amounts are null; the metered fare of 26.04 SGD remains charged, with 0.00 refunded to date; no driver compensation is payable. No clause of this policy produces a referral on a route deviation, so none is made.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

