    "explanation": "To both parties: this route-deviation dispute is decided on POL-RD-24's refund matrix (carrying v2.1 section 1.3). First, the deviation is measured the way POL-RD-22 requires — on the platform's recorded distances, not the trace: the actual route was 16.80 km (EV-TRIP-06003) against the recommended 15.30 km, a deviation of 1.50 km, above the 1.0 km tolerance. The 59-fix GPS trace (EV-GPS-06003) shows which route was taken and when (it leaves the ECP at the Fort Road exit at 17:58:49 and rejoins at Bedok South Road at 18:12:42), but it is not used to re-measure distance, because at 14.177 km it understates the route's length exactly as POL-RD-22 warns.\n\nSecond, the reroute was traffic-justified under POL-RD-23. LTA advisory LTA-TI-260923-1113 (EV-ADVIS-06003-01) records an ACCIDENT on the East Coast Parkway towards Changi after the Marine Parade exit, valid 17:34:22 to 18:49:22, which overlaps the trip window of 17:49:22 to 18:18:22. ACCIDENT falls within POL-RD-23's admissible 'incident' vocabulary. The artifact leaves the route-intersection question to me, and on its road, direction and location against the trip it resolves in favour of intersection: the recommended route runs along the ECP towards Changi and continues past the Marine Parade exit to the Bedok South Road exit — the very point at which the vehicle rejoined — so the advisory lies on the recommended route. The rider's point that the message says only 'Avoid lanes 2 and 3' and carries no severity does not help her: POL-RD-23 is satisfied by an incident, not only by a closure that shuts the road.\n\nThird, the driver informed the rider before the deviation and the rider agreed (POL-RD-21): MSG-06003-003 was sent 17:55:39 and read 17:55:48, and MSG-06003-004 'Sure no problem' was sent 17:56:14, both before the route_deviation_detected event at 17:58:49 (EV-CHAT-06003).\n\nWith traffic justification, prior notice and the rider's agreement, and a deviation over 1 km, POL-RD-24 row (a) applies and no refund is due. The rider's claims therefore fail: row (d) does not apply, because it requires the reroute to be not traffic-justified; the excess distance fare she points to (1.50 km x 0.72 SGD/km = 1.08 SGD, EV-FARE-06003) is the right figure only if row (d) or (b) applied, and neither does; and her claimed 5.00 SGD is unsupported on the policy's arithmetic in any event. Her alternative escalation under POL-GEN-26 also fails: every fact the matrix needs — the deviation distance, the notice, the rider's agreement and the traffic justification — is carried by a COMPLETE artifact at weight_multiplier 1.0, so no fact is unestablished and POL-GEN-02 does not lower the confidence cap.\n\nThe rider filed this dispute (case.authority.filing_frame), so NO_ACTION means her claim is not supported and the present state stands: the metered fare of 26.04 SGD remains charged and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00 (EV-FARE-06003). Both money fields are null, and no referral clause applies to a route deviation in this version. Confidence is 0.85, above the 0.80 POL-RD-25 requires for an AI route-deviation ruling, and the contested value of 5.00 SGD is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so this ruling is final."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
